{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhQCgxaqdLQVeYfS9yqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression is fixed: a stale worker can no longer finish, retry, delay or re-queue a recovered job, or renew its new owner's lock. The prevalidated command passes with my new test file added (8 files, 277 tests).\n\n## Root cause\nThree Lua scripts had lost their token comparison and only checked that *some* lock existed:\n\n- **`src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`**: the shared helper behind complete, fail, immediate retry, delayed retry, move-to-wait and move-to-waiting-children. It deleted whatever lock was there, so the \"lock mismatch\" branch was unreachable.\n- **`src/commands/extendLock-2.lua`**: single-job renewal overwrote the current owner's lock with the caller's token.\n- **`src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua`**: batch renewal did the same.\n\n## Fix\nEach script now compares the stored lock token to the caller's token — three one-line changes, no TypeScript changes.\n\n- **Stale finish/retry/delay**: rejected with the existing `JobLockMismatch` (-6) error before any job field, list, counter or event is touched.\n- **Missing lock**: still `JobLockNotExist` (-2).\n- **Stale renewal**: single-job returns `0`; batch returns the job id in the failed list, so the existing `lockRenewalFailed` event fires.\n- **Administrative calls**: the token `\"0\"` path that skips the lock is unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n- **New test**: `tests/stale_worker_lock.redis.test.ts` (9 cases) recovers a job through the real stalled checker, then checks each stale operation is rejected with state, counters, result, lock owner and event count unchanged, and that the owner can still renew and complete. 8 of the 9 fail with the fix stashed; all pass with it.\n- **Adjacent suites**: flow, delay, rate limiter and scripts tests pass.\n- **Two failures in `tests/script_loader.test.ts`**: both time out at 20s in the \"when initializing a RedisClient\" block. That block creates `new RedisConnection({})` with no port, so I believe it is looking for Redis on the default port rather than `REDIS_PORT`; I did not confirm that or run it on the unpatched tree.\n- **Build**: `npm run build` ran through to its final copy steps and the generated scripts were regenerated.\n\nThe Postgres backend already checks the token on these paths. I did not check the Python, Elixir, PHP or Rust ports."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":533,"cache_read_input_tokens":62202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":533},"output_tokens":737,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1dbf0a0c-dc90-4fd8-bb5e-42123f53969d","uuid":"61d99aa2-ee13-4a6a-9090-2bdf90dda6e9","timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:03:35.895Z","request_id":"req_011CfhQCgbWdCDQDwEHUrtM8"}
